<p>NOTE: There were 2.4 million more average common and equivalent shares outstanding than in 1996, due primarily to the effects of stock option exercises and other issuances related to employee benefit and dividend reinvestment plans.</p>
<p>Net income for the 1997 quarter was also $26,675,000, or $.28 per share, compared to net income for the 1996 quarter of $14,118,000, or $.15 per share, which included income from discontinued operations of $5,112,000, or $.05 per share, and a special charge of $12,000,000, or $.13 per share, for spin-off costs and management transition expenses.</p>
